# 96. FINAL DESIGN PRINCIPLE

The Tower is not designed as a collection of disconnected combat stages.

Each Floor represents a fragment of Aetheria.

Some Floors are personal journeys.

Some Floors require multiple Parties.

Some Floors force the Master to divide resources, protect different locations, and make decisions that affect every active Party.

```text
AETHERIA
   ↓
WORLD DESTROYED
   ↓
TOWER OF REBIRTH
   ↓
100 FLOORS
   ↓
EACH FLOOR = WORLD FRAGMENT
   ↓
EXPLORATION
   ↓
STORY
   ↓
CHARACTER
   ↓
SINGLE-PARTY OR MULTI-PARTY MISSION
   ↓
COMBAT
   ↓
EVENT
   ↓
BOSS / RAID
   ↓
RNG REWARD
   ↓
GAME STATE
   ↓
WORLD CHANGES
```

The **World Exploration System** allows the Master to understand the world **before it was destroyed**.

The **Dungeon System** allows the Master to experience the world **after its destruction**.

The **Event System** gives meaning to the choices, memories, relationships, and consequences that occur inside each Floor.

Together:

```text
                BEFORE
             AETHERIA
                 │
                 ▼
          WORLD EXPLORATION
                 │
                 ▼
             NIGHT OF RUIN
                 │
                 ▼
               AFTER
                 │
                 ▼
        TOWER OF REBIRTH
                 │
                 ▼
              100 FLOORS
                 │
                 ▼
       SINGLE-PARTY / MULTI-PARTY
                 │
                 ▼
              NYTHAR
                 │
                 ▼
          WORLD REBIRTH
```

> **The Master does not simply climb a Tower.**

> **The Master walks through the history, ruins, memories, and remaining fragments of an entire world.**

> **Every Floor is a piece of what Aetheria was.**

> **Some Floors are conquered by one Party.**

> **Some Floors require every Party to stand together.**

> **Every Event creates a consequence.**

> **Every decision can influence what Aetheria becomes.**
